---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const asideLinks = [
  { label: 'General information only', href: '#general-information-only' },
  { label: 'Physical safety', href: '#physical-safety' },
  { label: 'Data and backups', href: '#data-and-backups' },
  { label: 'Manufacturer tools', href: '#manufacturer-tools' },
  { label: 'No guaranteed outcome', href: '#no-guaranteed-outcome' },
  { label: 'External links', href: '#external-links' },
];
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  metaTitle="Disclaimer: Limits of the Troubleshooting Advice"
  description="FixProblemNow provides general troubleshooting information only. Read the limits on physical safety, data loss, manufacturer tools and guaranteed outcomes."
  canonical="/disclaimer/"
  eyebrow="Important"
  intro="The guides on this site are general troubleshooting information. They cannot account for every device, configuration, or fault, and they are not a substitute for qualified service."
  updated="2026-11-15"
  asideLinks={asideLinks}
  asideNote="If a device is unsafe, stop using it. A website cannot assess physical damage remotely."
>
  <h2 id="general-information-only">General information only</h2>
  <p>
    FixProblemNow publishes educational troubleshooting content. It does not provide a diagnosis for
    your specific device, a guarantee that a step will work, or a professional repair service. The
    site cannot see your device, inspect its hardware, read its logs, or verify its configuration.
    Menus, error messages, and behaviour can differ by model, region, software version, and
    organisation policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for deciding whether to follow a step, for backing up your data, and for
    stopping when a procedure exceeds your comfort or experience. If you are unsure, use the
    manufacturer’s support or a qualified technician.
  </p>

  <h2 id="physical-safety">Physical safety</h2>
  <div class="callout callout--important">
    <p class="callout__label">Stop for these signs</p>
    <p>
      Stop and disconnect power if it is safe to do so when you see smoke, sparks, a burning smell,
      a swollen battery, a cracked or leaking battery, or liquid inside a device. Do not open a power
      supply, microwave, or sealed battery enclosure. Contact a qualified repair service or, for
      fire or smoke, your local emergency service.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    Some guides mention opening a case, reseating components, or handling storage drives. Those
    steps can cause electric shock, burns, or damage even when described correctly. The presence of a
    step on this site is not a statement that it is safe for your device or your level of experience.
  </p>

  <h2 id="data-and-backups">Data and backups</h2>
  <p>
    Troubleshooting can erase data. Resets, reinstalls, disk repairs, partition changes, and storage
    diagnostics may remove files or make a failing drive harder to recover. Back up important data
    before any step that writes to storage, and keep a second copy if the data matters. A backup
    that has never been restored is not proven; check that you can open the backed-up files.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a drive is clicking, grinding, or has been physically damaged, stop using it and seek
    specialist data recovery. Repeated repair attempts can reduce what is recoverable.
  </p>

  <h2 id="manufacturer-tools">Manufacturer tools</h2>
  <p>
    Guides may link to manufacturer support pages, recovery images, firmware, and diagnostic tools.
    Those tools are controlled by the manufacturer, not by FixProblemNow. Download them only from the
    official domain, check the supported model, and read the manufacturer’s warnings before use.
    Unofficial firmware, modified system images, and third-party driver bundles are not recommended.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-guaranteed-outcome">No guaranteed outcome</h2>
  <p>
    A guide may fail because the fault is hardware-related, because a provider service is down,
    because an account is restricted, or because the device is running a version that behaves
    differently. The site does not promise that a problem will be fixed, that data will be
    recovered, or that a device will remain in warranty. No statement on the site should be read as
    a guarantee of a particular result.
  </p>

  <h2 id="external-links">External links</h2>
  <p>
    Links to third-party sites are provided for reference. FixProblemNow does not control those
    sites and is not responsible for their content, downloads, availability, or privacy practices.
    A link does not imply endorsement. See the <a href="/terms/">terms and conditions</a> for the
    full liability position and the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for sourcing
    standards.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
